1. pytorch_mppi  (version 0.9.1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:   https://github.com/LemonPi/pytorch_mppi
Maintainer: UM-ARM-Lab (University of Michigan Autonomous Robotic Manipulation Lab)
Author:     Sheng Zhong <zhsh@umich.edu>
License:    MIT
Added:      v2.8.4, for the MPPI optimizer-correctness parity check
            (docs/versions/v2.8.4/mppi_parity.md).

USED AS: a published reference implementation of information-theoretic MPPI.
Our cascaded (T, omega) dynamics, running cost and terminal cost are passed to it
as callbacks so that our own batched implementation can be checked against it at
matched hyperparameters. It is a REFERENCE ONLY -- it is not part of any scored
arm, no result is produced by it, and nothing in `src/frameworks/mppi/` other than
the parity module imports it.

